    "q-43770": {
      "dom_id": "step-q43770",
      "name": "Question 9",
      "problem": "Consider the vector space ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$ of all $2\\times 2$ matrices over $R$ and its subset $C=\\{[\\begin{aligned}a & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\,|\\,a\\in R\\}.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $C$ is closed under matrix addition\n\nII. $C$ is closed under scalar multiplication\n\nIII. $C$ is a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$\n\nIV. $C$ is **not** a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that a subset of a vector space is a subspace if it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. If ${A}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]$ and ${A}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]$ are two matrices from $C,$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1}+{A}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1}+{a}_{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is a matrix from $C.$ So, $C$ is closed under addition.\n\n- Statement II is true. If $A=[\\begin{aligned}a & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]$ is an element of $C$ and $k\\in R,$ then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}kA & =k[\\begin{aligned}a & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}ka & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is a matrix from $C.$ So, $C$ is closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement III is true, while statement IV is false. $C$ is a subspace because it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III only.\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
